cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WoundFrame in research, figures, analyses, presentations, or publications, please cite this software."
title: "WoundFrame: Reproducible scale-normalized wound image panels"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Maxim"
    given-names: "Ștefan-Rareș"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
abstract: >-
  WoundFrame is a reproducible Python workflow for standardizing longitudinal
  wound photographs to a common physical scale, extracting fixed physical
  fields of view, and generating subject-by-timepoint image panels while
  preserving calibration coordinates, processing settings, software versions,
  and SHA-256 source-image hashes.
keywords:
  - wound healing
  - image standardization
  - longitudinal imaging
  - preclinical imaging
  - reproducible research
  - wound photography
